From: Haoze <90812991+HaozeG@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:09:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] [shvla] iDMA backend: re-arm FSM in IDmaBe::update()
 (fixes K-tile-256 gemm hang)

Symptom: sh_gemm with tile K=256 (e.g. 128x128x256, 256x256x256) never
finishes; the DMA wait never returns and simulator memory grows to the cap.

Root cause: the release regulation change made IDmaBe::update() enqueue only
transfer_regulation_event instead of fsm_event. If can_accept_burst() is false
for a cycle and the regulation queue is empty, nothing wakes the FSM again, so
the current transfer never completes.

Fix: also enqueue fsm_event in update(). Carried in soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch
(hunk for pulp/idma/be/idma_be.cpp; verified to apply on the pristine nested
pulp file and to equal the patched working tree) and in the patched pulp tree.

Evidence: experiments/smolvla-e2e-baseline/LOG.md G3.1-diag3 (single-.so A/B:
deeploy idma .so fixes release; one-line source change in a rebuilt scratch
tree flips FAIL to PASS, 128x128x256 6174 ns, all 7 default shapes pass).
Candidate for an upstream report (gvsoc-pulp regulation-queue commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch b/soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch
index af52f9f..5ec394e 100644
--- a/soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch
+++ b/soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch
@@ -920,16 +920,19 @@ index 4e3a273..b82eab5 100644
  
  
  void IDmaBe::fsm_handler(vp::Block *__this, vp::ClockEvent *event)
-@@ -142,7 +191,7 @@ void IDmaBe::fsm_handler(vp::Block *__this, vp::ClockEvent *event)
+@@ -142,7 +191,10 @@ void IDmaBe::fsm_handler(vp::Block *__this, vp::ClockEvent *event)
  void IDmaBe::update()
  {
      // Check if any action should be taken in the next cycle from the FSM handler
 -    this->fsm_event.enqueue();
 +    this->transfer_regulation_event.enqueue();
++    // Also re-arm the FSM: it must be woken when can_accept_burst() was false and the
++    // regulation queue is empty, otherwise the current transfer never completes (hang).
++    this->fsm_event.enqueue();
  }
  
  
-@@ -169,6 +218,11 @@ void IDmaBe::write_data(uint8_t *data, uint64_t size)
+@@ -169,6 +220,11 @@ void IDmaBe::write_data(uint8_t *data, uint64_t size)
      transfer->dst += size;
      transfer->size -= size;
  
@@ -941,7 +944,7 @@ index 4e3a273..b82eab5 100644
      // And forward data.
      // Note that the source backend already checked that the destination was ready by calling
      // our is_ready_to_accept_data method
-@@ -181,7 +235,7 @@ void IDmaBe::write_data(uint8_t *data, uint64_t size)
+@@ -181,7 +237,7 @@ void IDmaBe::write_data(uint8_t *data, uint64_t size)
  void IDmaBe::ack_data(uint8_t *data, int size)
  {
      // Get the source backend protocol for the first transfer
@@ -950,7 +953,7 @@ index 4e3a273..b82eab5 100644
      IdmaBeConsumer *src_be = this->get_be_consumer(transfer->src, transfer->size, true);
  
      // And acknowledge the data to it so that the data can be freed
-@@ -199,8 +253,12 @@ void IDmaBe::ack_data(uint8_t *data, int size)
+@@ -199,8 +255,12 @@ void IDmaBe::ack_data(uint8_t *data, int size)
          this->trace.msg(vp::Trace::LEVEL_TRACE, "Finished burst (transfer: %p)\n", transfer);
  
          // And if so, remove it and notify the middle end
